# DDT - Debug an 8080 program

```text
B0:DDT PROGRAM.COM
```

## Inspect a program

At the dash prompt, D displays bytes and L lists 8080 instructions.
Addresses are hexadecimal. These commands examine the first 32 bytes of
a COM file, list instructions at its entry and show the registers:

```text
D100,11F
L100,10F
X
```

## Trace and leave

T traces one instruction. Use G when ready to execute the code. G0
returns to CP/M. Escape abandons the current interactive command. Use
[DASM](DASM.HLP) for Z80 disassembly.
